    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23114" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infantĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		infans, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to infants</i>
			or <i>little children</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					34, 2, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">blandimenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just. 17, 3, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uterus,</span>”
				<i>little</i>, <i>young</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 164, 12</span></i>
			.— Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infantĭlĭter</span></b> , <i>like a
				child</i>, <i><span class="en">Hier. Orig. in Jer. Hom. 1,
				p. 750</span></i>.</div>
